#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave test.
Full generalized Ohm's law: convection + Hall + resistive (eta*J) + electron
pressure gradient (grad Pe / (e n_e)) terms ALL active, in normalized CGS units.

Parameters match the whistler test (same ion-scale normalization so d_i ~ v_A ~ 1
in code units).  Here RESISTIVITY and ELECTRONTEMPERATURE are enabled so the
complete Ohm's-law field solver is exercised.  A moderate resistivity damps the
whistler, and the electron pressure gradient acts on the (weak) charge-density
fluctuations produced by particle noise; the test is a STABILITY / no-blow-up
regression check for the full solver, not a dispersion measurement.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Resistive term ON. Converted internally to code units
(etaCode = 4*pi*etaSI*Si2NoV*Si2NoL ~ 2.5e-3 here); damps the whistler so the
late-time transverse amplitude stays well below the seed.
#RESISTIVITY
1000000.0               etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Electron-pressure-gradient term ON (isothermal, gamma = 1). Converted
internally to code units (TeCode = TeEV*e/(mp*uNormSI^2) ~ 0.19 here); acts on
the charge-density fluctuations carried by particle noise.
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
5.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update: the explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale whistler mode. Because the compact curl operators annihilate the
exact Nyquist mode, the effective omega_max is far below the naive continuum
estimate and dt = 0.02 is RK4-stable even with nBSubcycle = 1 (verified:
identical whistler frequency for {1,4,8,16,32}).
#BSUBCYCLE
8                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
6.25                    dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
6.25                    TimeMax

#RUN

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB
